<InteriorLayout title="Privacy — OhWP Studios" description="How OhWP Studios uses information submitted through enquiries, project estimates, and other website forms."><main id="main"><section class="interior-mast"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Studio information / Privacy</p><h1>Your information.<br /><em>Used with purpose.</em></h1><p class="lede">This notice describes the information handled by the OhWP Studios website, a Hodges &amp; Co. Limited studio based in Accra, Ghana.</p></div></section><section class="wrap section-space editorial-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Contact &amp; requests</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:ohwpstudios@gmail.com">ohwpstudios@gmail.com ↗</a></div><div class="editorial-copy"><h2>What you share.</h2><p>Website forms collect the details you enter: contact information, organisation, project requirements, preferences, booking details, or collaboration information. Required fields are marked; optional fields can be left blank. We need the required details to process the relevant request.</p><p>We use submissions to respond, prepare project scopes, arrange consultations, and manage the resulting conversation. Enquiry forms also record basic form activity and browser information to help us understand form use.</p><h2>How it is processed.</h2><p>The website uses Cloudflare for hosting and data services. Email delivery uses Resend when configured. The project estimator may send your submitted project and contact information to Cloudflare Workers AI to generate a planning scope, with a rules-based fallback when AI is unavailable. Please do not submit credentials or confidential third-party information.</p><p>Saved estimates can produce a proposal link. Anyone with that link can read the proposal, including the project description and displayed client name or organisation. Share it only with intended collaborators.</p><h2>Your choices.</h2><p>To request access, a correction, deletion, or information about retention, contact the studio by email. We will review the request and explain any information that needs to remain for an active project, a contract, or a legal requirement. Newsletter messages have a separate unsubscribe flow.</p><p>You can also contact Ghana’s <a class="text-link" href="https://dpc.gov.gh/for-individuals/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Protection Commission ↗</a> about personal data rights. External sites linked from this website handle information under their own policies.</p></div></section></main></InteriorLayout>
